+/// Recolor terminal text matching a regular expression. Matching text is
+/// drawn in the given foreground color, always, regardless of the mouse or
+/// modifier state. Purely visual: a color rule never makes text clickable
+/// (use `link` for that), so pair the two when you want both.
+///
+/// The syntax is `link-color = <regex>,<color>`, e.g.
+/// `link-color = \bCEN-(12|40)\b,#30d158`. The color is the last field,
+/// so a comma inside the regex needs no escaping. When several rules match
+/// the same cell, the first one configured wins.
+///
+/// Text drawn with the inverse attribute, selected text and search matches
+/// keep their usual colors.
+///
+/// Setting this to an empty value clears every rule.
+@"link-color": RepeatableLinkColor = .{},
+
 /// Whether to start the window in a maximized state. This setting applies
